A||||5||BOILERMAKER||2.8 Hesitation - New problems||||1||
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||01-04-2000||09:08 AM||||OK, until I get my 3.1 built, I still have to drive the 2.8.  O wait, until FOCOA delivers the stock red paint for the valve covers and upper intake manifold, I have to drive my 2.8 also.  Funny how that works.  Gotta love FOCOA.  Hey guys, 3 weeks to deliver 2 cans of paint isn't bad is it????  They bite the big one.  OK, here's my problem.<P>Used to at constant speed I would get a "shimmy" or "sputter".  Recently I get this all the time now.  When the car is sitting still at idle it sounds good.  Now, when I accelerate (hard or light) or constant speed I get a lot of stammering and sputtering.<P>VRRRRRRMMMMMMMM(sputter)MMMMMMMMM(stammer)MMMMMMMMMM(puke on myself)MMMMMM.....etc.<P>Almost like it wants to backfire.  I took some carb cleaner and sprayed it into the throttle body, it wanted to die just like I thought it would.  I sprayed every vac line, EGR tube, everything else that could be a cause of it and nothing.  So, I replaced the O2 sensor, no dice.  I have replaced the TPS and that did nothing.<P>Gosh I can't wait until the 3.1 is done.  Anyone see something I am not?<p>[This message has been edited by BOILERMAKER (edited 01-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Thomas||01-04-2000||12:39 PM||||I´ve got the same problem.<BR>At my car it was one worn spark plug.<BR>1000 miles after changing of the spark plug.<BR>But it can be also:<BR>Distributor worn or cracked<BR>Worn cable<BR>wrong timing<P>Check the MAT sensor in the airfilter too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||01-04-2000||03:53 PM||||Check your cap and rotor, and especially your plug wires. Look at the places where the plug wires run side-by-side. Look for burned marks that might indicate the wires are cross-firing or firing to ground.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BOILERMAKER||01-05-2000||11:51 AM||||Just changed the cap last night (it was new, but went back with the old one).  Sprayed the plug wired to see if they were arching, nothing.  I don't know where this problem is.  <P>After all this, the problem is still there.  Jerky Jerky drive to work does not work.  Makes me mad even before I get to work which isn't good for answering work related questions.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||01-05-2000||03:07 PM||||A couple of things to check:<P>- Fuel filter<BR>- Fuel pump pressure<P>David.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||01-05-2000||06:29 PM||||my car did that too.<P>to fix it I changed the distributor cap and rotor, spak plug wires, and the ignition coil.<P>I know that it was in fact the coil that was making my car sputter because I changed it first........Then a week later it sputtered more and the spark plug wire was bad.....<BR>so it got a nice little tune up!||||reg||1
